-- Island translation template: every English text Island shows, 1372 in all.
-- Generated by tools/localization/gen_template.py from the L["..."] keys in the source.
-- Regenerate with:  python -I tools/localization/gen_template.py Island
-- Do not hand-edit this file. Regenerating overwrites it. Translate a copy instead.
--
-- This file is NOT loaded by the game (Island.toc does not list it). It is a reference list.
--
-- To translate:
--   1. Copy this file to Locales/<code>.lua, where <code> is the WoW locale
--      (koKR, zhCN, zhTW, deDE, frFR, esES, esMX, ruRU, ptBR, itIT).
--   2. Replace the first line with:
--        local L = select(2, ...).NewLocale("<code>") if not L then return end
--      NewLocale returns nil on other clients, so the file does nothing there.
--   3. Fill in the quotes on the right. Anything left as "" stays in English.
--   4. Keep every placeholder listed in a "keep placeholders" comment (%s, %d, %1$s, ...).
--      Numbered forms (%1$s, %2$s) may be reordered. Keep |c...|r colour codes and |n
--      line breaks as they are.
--   5. Add the file to Island.toc right after Locale.lua, as "Locales\<code>.lua".
--
-- Item, zone, spell and class names come from the game itself, already in your language,
-- so they are not listed here.


